  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f11e50891625fb39de472762aaaff23edf43372e37fcdf55d129da1125c0ff8a.png)\n\nFind the area of $\u25b3ABC.$ Round your answer to two decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}\u2061A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\u2220A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0441 & =AB=26, \\\\ b & =AC=22, \\\\ m\u2220A & ={11}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{11}^{\u2218}=0.190\\,809,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 22\\cdot 26\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{11}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =286\\cdot (0.190\\,809) \\\\  & \u224854.57,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places.",
